<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>The Conjurer's Guild</h1>
<p>For the conjurer profession see <a cmd='#'>Help Conjurers</a>
</p><p>The Conjurer Guild is described by some as the elite of magic with the
cunning to match. It is certainly true they have more than their share
of geniuses, Magical powers combined with the brains and charisma to
convince elementals and even devils to do their bidding, makes this
Guild an excellent choice for the budding mage. However, their members
are also known for their lack of stamina and weakness of arm. This class
gives your character good possibilities for learning magic spells. Some of
these spells can defend you from the hostile world surrounding you and even
make some think twice before attacking.
</p><p>The guild is the College of Arcane Arts in Midgaard, just south of 
Cathedral Square. Its head is Rafizir the Archchancellor, in his office at 
the back of the College. Spells are taught in the Tower of Arcane, skills 
in the Main Lecture Hall, weapons in the Tower of Mundane and abilities in 
the Library.
</p><p>To join, stand before Rafizir and type <a cmd='#'>join</a>. Followers of the faith 
can't master the science of magic: healers, druids, necromancers, 
paladins, dark knights and rangers are turned away. First you must prove 
yourself worthy by finishing the Conjurer's Guild quest: Mr Backspindle, 
the gardener in the College gardens, wants the head of Xad, the Master of 
Conjuring at the Academy. To leave the guild, insult the Master; but a 
member who is banished can never come back.
</p><p>The first time a member bows to Rafizir, he gives a Spellweaver Charm: 
grip it in a fight and it summons a creature to fight at your side for a 
short while. Type <a cmd='#'>title</a> before him for a new title as you rise in the 
guild.
</p><p><br />
